# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""PANEL BANK, part 1: the eight-event foreseeability panel + controls, in EN/DE/FR.

Design rules (enforced by panel_bank.py before freezing):
  * SUBJECT (loaded stem): strictly pre-event vocabulary and knowledge, forward-framed. No post-event
    coinages, no proper nouns that only exist after the event.
  * TARGET: the ex-post truth, phrased with as few proper nouns as possible (small lexical share).
  * NEUTRAL: a de-loaded frame that still grammatically licenses the target (calibration).
  * Each item is a dict lang -> (subject, target, neutral); translations are meaning- and length-parallel.

Estimator (see PREREGISTRATION_FORESIGHT_v2.md):
  in-family events:  Dconc = strain_pre - strain_anchor   (same tokenizer; lexical floor cancels exactly)
  modern-anchored :  XS    = strain_pre - strain_modern, bridge-corrected by the in-family offset
                     offset_lang = mean over anchor-1929 event items of (strain_1929 - strain_modern)
"""

# event -> metadata. "pre" = foresight model(s) (the LAST entry is the headline pre model);
# "anchor" = hindsight anchor for Dconc ("modern" => bridge-corrected XS).
